# Git workflow — Website Version branches

**Status:** Dual-branch website versioning is active. The old “main only / no `dev`” rule is superseded for this repo.

Authority: `.cursor/rules/website-version-management.mdc`

## Branches

- **`main`** = Website Version 1 (production)
- **`website-v2`** = Website Version 2 (development)

## Rules

- Commit Version 1 work only on `main`.
- Commit Version 2 work only on `website-v2`.
- Never develop V2 on `main`.
- Never merge `website-v2` → `main` without explicit user approval.
- Do **not** recreate a generic `dev` branch; use `website-v2` / future `website-v3`.
- Short-lived feature branches only when the user asks; merge into the correct version branch.

## Deploy

- Deploy Version 1 → only when user says **Deploy Version 1** (from `main`)
- Deploy Version 2 → only when user says **Deploy Version 2** (from `website-v2`)
- Build-only Webdock: `scripts/deploy-website-build-only.ps1`
